+## Setup — run it from a clean checkout
+
+### Prerequisites
+- Docker (with Compose)
+- Python 3.10+
+- `psql` is optional (handy for ad-hoc queries); the loader uses `psycopg`.
+
+### 1. Start SereneDB
+
+```bash
+docker compose up -d          # starts SereneDB on localhost:7890, mounts ./data -> /data
+docker ps                     # confirm the 'serenedb' container is running
+```
+
+<details>
+<summary>Equivalent without Compose</summary>
+
+```bash
+docker run -d --name serenedb -p 7890:7890 \
+  -v serenedb-data:/var/lib/serenedb \
+  -v "$PWD/data":/data \
+  serenedb/serenedb
+```
+</details>
+
+> **Why the `./data` mount matters:** SereneDB reads files from *its own* filesystem.
+> Mounting `./data` to `/data` lets the loader read the downloaded logs with
+> `read_csv('/data/BGL.log')`. Without it, loading fails.
+
+### 2. Install Python dependencies
+
+```bash
+python -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate   # optional
+pip install -r requirements.txt
+```
+
+### 3. Download + load the corpus
+
+```bash
+python load_data.py
+```
+
+This will:
+1. Download `BGL.zip` and `OpenStack.tar.gz` from Zenodo into `./data/` (≈770 MB, skipped if already present).
+2. Create the `bgl`, `openstack` and `team_ownership` tables (idempotent — it drops and recreates).
+3. Parse the raw log lines into typed columns, including a real `ts TIMESTAMP`.
+4. Verify the loaded counts match the expected totals and print per-component / per-team / time-range summaries.
+
+Expected on success:
+
+```
+bgl: 4,747,963 rows (expected 4,747,963) -> OK
+openstack: 207,820 rows (expected 207,820) -> OK
+Done. All row counts match.
+```
+
+> **Loading from a container running elsewhere?** Point the loader at it with
+> `SERENEDB_HOST` / `SERENEDB_PORT` env vars, and make sure that host has the same
+> `./data` folder mounted at `/data`.
+
+### 4. Start the agent workflow (MCP server)
+
+```bash
+python mcp_server.py
+```
+
+Then connect your coding assistant to it as an MCP (stdio) server. For **Claude Code**:
+
+```bash
+claude mcp add log-insights -- python /absolute/path/to/mcp_server.py
+```
+
+For **Cursor / Codex / other clients**, add a stdio MCP server that runs
+`python mcp_server.py` from this repo. The agent then discovers the five tools below
+and answers questions for each role. See **[REPORT.md](REPORT.md)** for the exact
+questions and the evidence behind each answer.
 
