+## Schema
+
+Both tables keep the original fields **and** a parsed `ts TIMESTAMP` and `line_no`
+(stable ordering) so time filters, nearby-event lookups and trends are correct.
+
+**`openstack`** — `line_no, src_file, ts, log_date, log_time, pid, level, component, module, content`
+(`component` is derived from the source log file: `nova-api`, `nova-compute`, `nova-scheduler`.)
+
+**`bgl`** — `line_no, ts, alert_flag, epoch, date_str, node, time_str, node_repeat, log_type, component, level, content`
+(`ts` is built from BGL's local time field; `alert_flag` is `-` for non-alert lines.)
+
+**`team_ownership`** — `dataset, component, team_name, lead_contact`
+
+---
+
+## Ownership table
+
+`ownership.csv` is a **fictional** mapping that ties the components of both datasets into
+one platform org, so the team-lead and manager answers can group counts by owning team.
+It is loaded into `team_ownership` and joined on `(dataset, component)`.
+
+| Dataset | Component | Team | Lead contact |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| openstack | nova-api | Compute Platform Team | compute-lead@platform.internal |
+| openstack | nova-compute | Hypervisor Operations | hypervisor@platform.internal |
+| openstack | nova-scheduler | Core Scheduling Team | scheduler@platform.internal |
+| bgl | KERNEL / SERPENT | Core OS Team | os-team@platform.internal |
+| bgl | APP | Application Runtime Team | apps@platform.internal |
+| bgl | HARDWARE | Data Center Ops | dc-ops@platform.internal |
+| bgl | DISCOVERY / BGLMASTER | Cluster Operations | cluster-ops@platform.internal |
+| bgl | MMCS / CMCS | Machine Management Team | machine-mgmt@platform.internal |
+| bgl | LINKCARD | Interconnect Team | interconnect@platform.internal |
+| bgl | MONITOR | Monitoring Team | monitoring@platform.internal |
+
+Components not present in the table fall back to *"Unassigned / Core Infrastructure"* in
+the team aggregation, so nothing is silently dropped.
